// error: `isEmpty` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `isEmpty`, not `isEmpty()`
// error: `trim` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `trim`, not `trim()`
// error: `isOk` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `isOk`, not `isOk()`
// error: `swap` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `swap`, not `swap()`
// error: `isDigit` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `isDigit`, not `isDigit()`
// An option's, a string's, a result's, an either's and a char's accessors are declared without a
// parameter list, so a call with `()` is an error naming the fix.

main()
    println(Some(1).isEmpty())
    println(" a ".trim())
    val r: Result[int, string] = Ok(1)
    println(r.isOk())
    val e: Either[string, int] = Right(2)
    println(e.swap())
    println('7'.isDigit())
